\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Repeat-mask residual already measured on stored checkpoints (no new training). ``P0-protocol'' scores every exported KC-row; ``clean'' masks repeat-row targets (\texttt  {--mask-repeats}). The $+$0.0101 residual on QKC-T fold~0 is the drop from scoring all expanded rows to scoring the masked remainder---the pyKT repeat-format effect \cite  {liu2022pykt}---not an attempt-level collapse and not a history-side de-duplication. The same recipe on folds~1--2 yields $+$0.0094 and $+$0.0091. A Q$\leftarrow $KC checkpoint without the $\Delta t$ branch under a different window rule (\texttt  {last}, $L$ budget of that run) is near null ($-$0.0007); that row does \emph  {not} isolate the time branch from the window rule. An older chunked no-time residual (\texttt  {v4q\_clean}, $\approx {-}0.0003$) is not the Table~\ref {tab:auc-xes3g5m} Q$\leftarrow $KC run. On the fold-0 test export every repeat row has raw $\Delta t{=}0$ ($183{,}741$ rows; $14.4\%$ of P0-protocol targets). We have not yet run attempt-level collapse; headline AUCs remain repeat-target-masked KC-expanded, not question-level.}}{21}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:protocol-residual}{{4}{21}{Repeat-mask residual already measured on stored checkpoints (no new training). ``P0-protocol'' scores every exported KC-row; ``clean'' masks repeat-row targets (\texttt {--mask-repeats}). The $+$0.0101 residual on QKC-T fold~0 is the drop from scoring all expanded rows to scoring the masked remainder---the pyKT repeat-format effect \cite {liu2022pykt}---not an attempt-level collapse and not a history-side de-duplication. The same recipe on folds~1--2 yields $+$0.0094 and $+$0.0091. A Q$\leftarrow $KC checkpoint without the $\Delta t$ branch under a different window rule (\texttt {last}, $L$ budget of that run) is near null ($-$0.0007); that row does \emph {not} isolate the time branch from the window rule. An older chunked no-time residual (\texttt {v4q\_clean}, $\approx {-}0.0003$) is not the Table~\ref {tab:auc-xes3g5m} Q$\leftarrow $KC run. On the fold-0 test export every repeat row has raw $\Delta t{=}0$ ($183{,}741$ rows; $14.4\%$ of P0-protocol targets). We have not yet run attempt-level collapse; headline AUCs remain repeat-target-masked KC-expanded, not question-level}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Two-sided paired $t$-tests on unrounded validation $\Delta $ (\texttt  {b8\_holm\_credit\_tests.json}; $m{=}3$ Holm--Bonferroni). The operating rule is $5/5$ seeds with $\Delta \mathrm  {val}\ge {+}0.002$; it is not $H_0{:}\,\mu _\Delta =0$ and not $H_0{:}\,\mu _\Delta \le 0.002$. Holm is applied to the two-sided raw $p$ (a previous draft printed Holm on one-sided $p$). History-only, M4, and P4 are judged only by the $5/5$ rule.}}{21}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:credit-stats}{{5}{21}{Two-sided paired $t$-tests on unrounded validation $\Delta $ (\texttt {b8\_holm\_credit\_tests.json}; $m{=}3$ Holm--Bonferroni). The operating rule is $5/5$ seeds with $\Delta \mathrm {val}\ge {+}0.002$; it is not $H_0{:}\,\mu _\Delta =0$ and not $H_0{:}\,\mu _\Delta \le 0.002$. Holm is applied to the two-sided raw $p$ (a previous draft printed Holm on one-sided $p$). History-only, M4, and P4 are judged only by the $5/5$ rule}{table.5}{}}
